{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents","id":1009346,"title":"Can a san animal become an Exigents.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-28T08:41:58-08:00","id":1009346,"title":"Can a san animal become an Exigents.","content":"Is it possible for a god to gift an intelligent animal (i.e. a non-human equal) with an Exigent exaltation, as the Exigent seem very tightly linked to the nature of the god giving it.<br /> <br /> i.e. Lazy the Sloth god decides to give up a significant portion of its power to Exalt Flash the Sloth. Flash suddenly finds that he has mirarulus powers, such as Sloth Speed Bump, or Prana of Making a Glorious Poo Before Being Eaten by a Predator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","name":"zylosan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T08:50:51-08:00","id":1009348,"title":"","content":"The rule with Exigents is &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Can Exigents be more powerful than a Solar?&quot; &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;<br /> &quot;Can a Volcano god have an Exigent with ice powers?&quot; &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;<br /> &quot;Can the least god of a bowl of rice Exalt someone as an Exigent?&quot; &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:00:09-08:00","id":1009354,"title":"","content":"the heavenly power of &quot;Making a Glorious Poo Before Being Eaten by a Predator&quot; sounds amazing<br /> <br /> hell, that gives me an idea for a temple that would get a strange kind of pilgrims: Constipated pilgrims.<br /> <br /> <br /> The temple of Lazy the Sloth god, known well in certain circles of the east, as the go-to place if you simply cannot get a bowel movement. Pilgrims from across the east travel to the temple and dray for swift and merciful release.<br /> <br /> They often get it too - hence the popularity of the temple - but what is rarely spoken of, is that this blessing also incurs an attack of a wild animal that would normally eat sloths, though thankfully the monks of the temple have set up a very nice side-business selling increasingly worn albeit well-maintained buff jackets and wooden clubs with nails in them to find off whatever might come after you. Pray that its a large bird of prey, not a poisonous snake or a jaguar.<br /> <br /> Also there is a lively local jaguar-pelt trading post near the temple, for no apparent reason","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:11:17-08:00","id":1009359,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo\">Kyeudo</a>: </b>Not to be a dick but &quot;You can if you want to&quot; is kind of a useless answer in an RPG. Because anything can be if the GM wants it to. We have rules to provide a degree of mutual structure to guide what can be expected.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla\">webkilla</a>: That is totally epic.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","name":"zylosan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:24:00-08:00","id":1009364,"title":"","content":"I would most likly rule that you have to be a human. A human of any flavor(wyld tainted, beastman, cool ranch. ect.), but still a human. You can, of course, do whatever you wish in your game.<br /> <br /> Things that I would keep in mind. The exigence, unless stolen, is given by the UCS to the god wanting to use it. The exigence is a super emergency, last line of defence, hail mary kind of thing to ask for. It will kill most gods who use it, and there is no way to know if it will kill this god until it is done. <br /> <br /> All that said, the best way to make an exigent is to first make a fully fleshed out god for it to be based on. That will inform a lot about what this particular exigent is capable of, and how they go about doing things.<br /> <br /> Is this for a PC or NPC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:30:56-08:00","id":1009367,"title":"","content":"I'd say tinkering with an exigence to the point it will work with a non-human is possible, but totally voids the warranty. So we're talking black-market stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:31:29-08:00","id":1009368,"title":"","content":"Since the Exigent book hasn't came out, &quot;You can if you want to&quot; is pretty much your only answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:34:18-08:00","id":1009369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009348#post1009348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule with Exigents is &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Can Exigents be more powerful than a Solar?</b>&quot; &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;<br /> &quot;Can a Volcano god have an Exigent with ice powers?&quot; &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;<br /> &quot;Can the least god of a bowl of rice Exalt someone as an Exigent?&quot; &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally I think it is more &quot;Is there a good reason for this? Then yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> And to address the bolded part specifically, there is no god with the purview and themes of &quot;generically more powerful than the UCS/Solars&quot;. An exigent can possibly compete at the &quot;Solar level&quot; in abilities that fall under their themes, and can definitly outclass a Solar at something like walking among dreams or stuff that.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can do what you want in your games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:37:52-08:00","id":1009371,"title":"","content":"Presumably the Solars represent the largest amount of power Conky can fit in an exaltation already. If you try to make something bigger with an exigence it probably pops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:50:45-08:00","id":1009376,"title":"","content":"I don't think Exigents will be open to animals by default, though I can see a good case for a wilderness-god or goddess of the hunt attaching Exaltation to a phenomenal and singular animal, such that the human who bonds with it inherits the Exigence.<br /> <br /> (It'd be like the artifact-based example, but would instead be keyed off a Familiar!)<br /> <br /> Just plain making an animal Exalt, though? Sounds about as likely as Toriyama publishing a Namekian cookbook; just because the <i>rules</i> for Exigents are intended to be open-ended enough for all manner of <i>players</i> to cook up whatever wacky Exalt types they want, that doesn't mean the Exigents themselves will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-28-2016, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T10:16:22-08:00","id":1009383,"title":"","content":"I don't know about san beasts, but can beastmen breed themselves into being nearly indistinguishable from animals? You could get a really similar effect that way I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T10:38:49-08:00","id":1009388,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is the default for how most exaltations for but look at it this way:<br /> <br /> 1) Celestial Exaltation takes a human body and human soul and powers it with the power of the Incarne.<br /> 2) Terrestrial Exaltation takes a human bloodline and human soul and powers it with the power of the Terrestrial Dragons.<br /> 3) Alchemical exaltation takes a lump a clay lined with magical materials, the soul of a hero, and a spark of power.<br /> 4) Liminal exaltation takes a collection of dead corpses, some unknown parts (presumably some kind of human soul), and some unknown power of the Dark Mother<br /> <br /> So given all these things, I don't see why a god couldn't obtain a human soul, attach it to an exigence, and shove the construct into a san animal. Exigents are supposed to be unique... so why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 11-28-2016, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:06:58-08:00","id":1009396,"title":"","content":"One of the core ideas is that the process of Exaltation requires a human soul. This is why Dragon Kings, animals and the like can't actually Exalt. They don't possess human souls. I would say the same is true of the Exigency - it is a specific process of Exaltation and to my understanding you couldn't use it to &quot;Exalt&quot; an animal, or a Dragon King or anything else that the other, more traditional Exaltations would not normally work on.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, it's possible that the Ata-beasts in Halta have human souls - it's never been made clear, but it seems like a reasonable thing for an ST to introduce if you want to make a cool animal Exalt. It seems rather unlikely however that san-beasts do as they are only partially sentient.<br /> <br /> Further, it's very easy to imagine &quot;Exalted-ish&quot; methods by which a spirit could &quot;empower&quot; an animal in a way that makes it very similar to the process of Exaltation (giving it an Essence pool, access to Charms, and perhaps human-level intelligence). This would not be Exaltation but rather a different process that leads to a result which is nearly identical for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> Of course, at the end of the day your ST is the one in charge and Exalted is his or her game. If she or he wants to allow you to play a Solar sloth then you can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-28-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:59:41-08:00","id":1009417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009369#post1009369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An exigent can possibly compete at the &quot;Solar level&quot; in abilities that fall under their themes, and can definitly outclass a Solar at something like walking among dreams or stuff that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's possible that there will be Exigents whose power is not so situational. It seems to be inherent to what is going in when the developers ask us to consider the god in person, rather than the portfolio.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Chosen of one volcano god has powers that have special or exclusive functionality in the presence of volcanos, and the Chosen of a different volcano god has powers that are analogous to the nature of a volcano.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's possible for something closer to the latter to have about the same strength as a given example of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bPart of the value of Exigents is that you can get away with that kind of thing, because it is a confined instance of it that does not warp the setting in the way that having a group consisting of hundreds of Exalted having such power would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009383#post1009383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about san beasts, but can beastmen breed themselves into being nearly indistinguishable from animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with no, especially considering that it's unlikely that any beast folk will continue procreating with animals after the progenitor of the line.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, even assuming that they did, I would find the premise to be running off of a logic that doesn't really include the idea of eventually eliminating human traits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:00:07-08:00","id":1009418,"title":"","content":"I agree with the meat balloon theory as far as making an exigent more powerful than a solar. DBs existed in past editions because Gaia couldn't empower something directly without making things blow up and Celestials invested quite a bit of their power into their exalts (and the Incarna are almost always described as being so far above standard gods that it seems inappropriate to have them in the same category). <br /> <br /> As to animals? I don't think it would work because of the soul thing and also if you forgive the 2ed reference I am rather fond of the example of the one crazy solar that turned into an cthulu-thing and had her powers begin to malfunction immediately and her spawn couldn't seem to exalt despite having human souls. That being said Exalts are weird in the first place and Exigents are essentially even weirder exalts so I wouldn't be surprised if an exigent had the ability to turn into a sacred animal of their patron or something of the sort...<br /> <br /> Now I want a Panther Exigent that rules a bizarrely advanced country surrounded by extremely poor countries that is inexplicably self-sufficient...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:08:41-08:00","id":1009424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009418#post1009418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the meat balloon theory as far as making an exigent more powerful than a solar. DBs existed in past editions because Gaia couldn't empower something directly without making things blow up and Celestials invested quite a bit of their power into their exalts (and the Incarna are almost always described as being so far above standard gods that it seems inappropriate to have them in the same category).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've got things the wrong way around there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:24:23-08:00","id":1009426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009424#post1009424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you've got things the wrong way around there.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I'm terrible with wording so I'm honestly curious because I meant that the Incarna rank somewhere between Primordials and gods rather than being above average gods (somewhere around the stronger third circles).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:53:38-08:00","id":1009439,"title":"","content":"Gaia didn't personally empower humans herself - we don't <i>have</i> the why of it, so &quot;it would just be too much power&quot; is just an assumption. And not necessarily a very fitting one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:05:20-08:00","id":1009444,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth I meant the <i>exigence</i> would pop. Cos it's sol-based and why would sol use a second-tier container with his <i>own</i> essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:07:49-08:00","id":1009447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009439#post1009439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia didn't personally empower humans herself - we don't <i>have</i> the why of it, so &quot;it would just be too much power&quot; is just an assumption. And not necessarily a very fitting one.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair I did note that it was an explanation from 2ed but it is the only info we have and I thought that it was fairly unoffensive by 2ed standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:00:06-08:00","id":1009526,"title":"","content":"We do have various hints that a (n ex-)primordial trying to empower mortals directly can have odd results in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:24:59-08:00","id":1009532,"title":"","content":"Do we have any evidence that a Yozi has ceased to be a Primordial? That being imprisoned has somehow changed them <i>from</i> someone who existed at the beginning of Time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:29:42-08:00","id":1009535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009359#post1009359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo\">Kyeudo</a>: </b>Not to be a dick but &quot;You can if you want to&quot; is kind of a useless answer in an RPG. Because anything can be if the GM wants it to. We have rules to provide a degree of mutual structure to guide what can be expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents are all about breaking the rules. They exist solely to justify &quot;build your own Exalt&quot; in the setting without needing much shoehorning. &quot;If you think so, then yes&quot; is about as close to a solid answer as you can get with this unmapped territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009369#post1009369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to address the bolded part specifically, there is no god with the purview and themes of &quot;generically more powerful than the UCS/Solars&quot;. An exigent can possibly compete at the &quot;Solar level&quot; in abilities that fall under their themes, and can definitly outclass a Solar at something like walking among dreams or stuff that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who cares about purview? That just defines themes, not magnitude of impact. Sol Invictus may be the biggest, baddest god in the sky, but he made hundreds of Exalts and didn't put his all into the effort. A god who throws his all into a single Exalt could very well produce an Exigent with more raw power than any single Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:37:28-08:00","id":1009539,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen anything that said that the UCS didn't give it his full effort when creating the Solars. And I don't necessarily agree that you could create one as powerful and more general than a Solar, but in the purview that is their specialty, I wouldn't be against it. But not just because the God in question is 'only' creating 1 Exalt.<br /> <br /> Though what I like most about Exigence is that it's now my preferred head-canon that the Incarnae are still weakened by the effort of creating their Exalted, and that's why they spend most of their time lounging around Yu Shan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:43:43-08:00","id":1009541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broken Masque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009539#post1009539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen anything that said that the UCS didn't give it his full effort when creating the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen several things that explicitly say he <i>did. </i>Seriously, could you really create the Solar Exaltations with anything less?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:12:42-08:00","id":1009555,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun is still alive, therefore he did not give it his all. If he had given everything to making the Solars, then he would have nothing left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:27:25-08:00","id":1009562,"title":"","content":"By that logic, any athlete who doesn't die while playing isn't giving it his all, and Michael Jordan is a hack.<br /> <br /> No, my assumption for Exigence is that a god generally doesn't decide how much of himself he wants to put into it (unless it's a &quot;dirty bomb,&quot; but that's another story) - the word &quot;Exigent&quot; implies urgency and immediacy, so whatever problem the god needs it for, he needs it enough that he invests to the point where he's<i> risking </i>his very life.<br /> <br /> If Ahlat uses the Exigence and lives, it's not because he put less of himself into it than Ten Sheaves had, but rather because he's lucky/hardy/potent enough to survive exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-28-2016, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:09:23-08:00","id":1009581,"title":"","content":"Exigents are Exalted, but Celestial Exalted are not Exigents. The Sun did not employ the Exigence to create the Solar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:26:38-08:00","id":1009584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009562#post1009562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that logic, any athlete who doesn't die while playing isn't giving it his all, and Michael Jordan is a hack.</div> </div> </div> </div>John Henry probably agrees with that. If you want to be the best, you can't hold anything back.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T21:29:52-08:00","id":1009633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009359#post1009359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Kyeudo</a>: </b>Not to be a dick but &amp;quot;You can if you want to&amp;quot; is kind of a useless answer in an RPG. Because anything can be if the GM wants it to. We have rules to provide a degree of mutual structure to guide what can be expected.]</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't actually have the rules yet in this case, but Kyeudo's answer seems consistent with what we do know, which is that the Exigence is there largely to let Storytellers add whatever Exalts they want to the game; the &quot;structure&quot; they provide isn't a power curve or a set of strict limitations, but rather an in-setting mechanism to explain where one-off Exaltations come from. As such, &quot;you can if you want&quot; does appear to be the actual authorial intent.<br /> <br /> All that said, in my Creation I could totally see an Exigent Ata-Beast, but probably not a San-Beast, because ata-beasts are basically people so sure, but the niche of &quot;uniquely powerful magic semi-intelligent animal&quot; would be filled other ways.<br /> <br /> FWIW, I could also see an Exigent Dragon-King; I think that's a cooler way to explain/build/play an Olichilike (sp) than a random spirit with a possession Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T22:22:34-08:00","id":1009641,"title":"","content":"When it comes to developing the mythos of creating Exalted, I would incline more to the idea that a god who is sacrificed is handling something so beyond them that they're consumed (doing so regardless for the sake of a higher ideal), rather than it being a question of how much effort you put into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to be the best, you can't hold anything back.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think of how good advice for running a race is to pace yourself early on, so that you'll have a lot of energy at the end to outrun everybody who tired themselves out at the start.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr how in certain kinds of sport fighting, &quot;not holding anything back&quot; means you injure yourself at least as badly as your opponent.<br /> <br /> \u200bNone of these examples are really significant to a description of mythology, but I am bemused by the general sentiment.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe story of John Henry is folklore verging on propaganda, and not something I find to be an especially useful reference point.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot to mention all kinds of endeavours, even ones based on physical prowess, in which working to the point of death or disfigurement is not only not useful, but not really possible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009426#post1009426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? I'm terrible with wording so I'm honestly curious because I meant that the Incarna rank somewhere between Primordials and gods rather than being above average gods (somewhere around the stronger third circles).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat was my mistake for not selecting my quote more carefully; I was talking about the line concerning Dragon Blooded and Gaia.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven then, I considered later that it was likely that you meant &quot;this was what the Edition depicted&quot; rather than &quot;this is why the Edition depicted it&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:27:08-08:00","id":1009682,"title":"","content":"We also have to remember that Exigents can run the full range of power levels... from the equivalent of the Dragon-Blooded to as powerful as the Solars. A God that would be consumed creating an Exigent as powerful as a Solar may not be entirely consumed if it chose to create an Exigent with equivalent power to a Dragon-Blood. Some Gods may not be able to create an Exigent as powerful as a Solar even if they give their existence to the process... and may have to settle for an Exigent somewhere lower on the power scale.<br /> <br /> It all really depends on what the God creating an Exigent needs... does he need a Champion as powerful as a Solar at the cost of his existence... or would an Exigent of lesser power suffice (giving him the chance to survive the process). Not every God who is given the chance to create an Exigent will create the most powerful one they can... but rather will only create one as powerful as they need.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for Kyeudo's responses... while all answers are a response to a question, not all responses are answers. His response was so vague that it didn't actually answer anything... but seemed to provide the only answer anyone could expect. Just because someone can think of something or have a need for something, doesn't mean that an Exigent can fill that roll. Yes, Exigents will fill the role of custom Exalts... but that doesn't mean one can create the most powerful and broken splat that can beat anything the setting has with just it's pinky finger... there will be guidelines and limitations to what can be done... and what it will cost. So no... &quot;if you can think it then yes&quot; is not an acceptable answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:30:06-08:00","id":1009684,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2243_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2243\" data-vbnamecard=\"2243\">Shadowstripe</a>: That assumes that a given god can even decide how much of itself it's going to invest - do we have any evidence that's the case?<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd prefer if gods seeking something <i>named for how dire one's need of it is</i> to not be able to just phone it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-29-2016, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:43:25-08:00","id":1009687,"title":"","content":"I would answer no-ish, mostly because the game's rules just aren't really designed for playing animals, or non-people generally. And the game is <i>about</i> people, heroic people, not heroic animals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:50:09-08:00","id":1009711,"title":"","content":"In early 1e the Animal Avatars were empowered by Gaia in a manner compared to Exaltation but as time's gone on they seem to have been repackaged more as animal gods. I'd point a player who wanted to be an Animal Exalt with the powers of being an exceptional animal at that, it'd probably use the Exigent book if it was available but not the Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:08:26-08:00","id":1009755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009687#post1009687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would answer no-ish, mostly because the game's rules just aren't really designed for playing animals, or non-people generally. And the game is <i>about</i> people, heroic people, not heroic animals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>More than that, I think there's a question of intent and practicality.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf one is referring to the san animals of Halta specifically, then in a game focused on Halta specifically, I would say that it can be reasonably serviceable. Perhaps a bit of a challenge, some things may strain a bit at times, but apart from that being a description of Exalted in general, animals are at least playable enough to facilitate Lunars turning into them, and different people have different ideas about how Other the intellects of san animals should be in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200bConversely, in games where they've gone rather far afield from somewhere like Halta, I would wonder at the possibility of using the idea primarily for the sake of novelty, in which case, well, people can still do whatever they want, I would just question whether or not this is something that will be very fulfilling or last long. <br /> <br /> \u200bIf a person has a very very intriguing character idea to actually take advantage of the distinction, then I'm sure they can keep it going.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That assumes that a given god can even decide how much of itself it's going to invest</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it necessarily does; I think the statement &quot;the god will create the most powerful Exalt that they need&quot; does not necessarily attribute a conscious decision to the process.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll of this being said, I think the idea behind the mythology that the books will present to us will attribute occasions in which Exigents are at the height of their potential power will be less about the depth of sacrifice of the god involved and more by the grace of the Unconquered Sun. That's not saying that the Sun is making a conscious decision either, rather that it's just a boost that is made available by the whole thing using power created and bestowed by him.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think one thing that the internal logic of the setting might contain that could discount the idea of it being based off of the depth of one's sacrifice is that I think that, for most gods, being consumed utterly is a fairly low bar to jump. That is to say that if any salt god or dog of the unbroken earth creates any kind of Exalt, they will be used up in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:25:48-08:00","id":1009770,"title":"","content":"Honestly if I had a player who wanted to play Sir Bearington I don't think I could bring myself to say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:53:27-08:00","id":1009838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009682#post1009682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs for Kyeudo's responses... while all answers are a response to a question, not all responses are answers. His response was so vague that it didn't actually answer anything... but seemed to provide the only answer anyone could expect. Just because someone can think of something or have a need for something, doesn't mean that an Exigent can fill that roll. Yes, Exigents will fill the role of custom Exalts... but that doesn't mean one can create the most powerful and broken splat that can beat anything the setting has with just it's pinky finger... there will be guidelines and limitations to what can be done... and what it will cost. So no... &quot;if you can think it then yes&quot; is not an acceptable answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your Storyteller thinks that such an Exigent serves his narrative needs or that giving such power to a player would create the kind of game he wants to run, then it is perfectly within the orbit of the Exigence to introduce such an Exalt to the game.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Celestial God of Victory burns herself out to empower a mortal general to triumph against all odds because she could not bear the thought of him dying defeated and that creates an Exalt with powers to literally say &quot;I win&quot; on nearly anything. Maybe this general is now threatening the design of fate because of his rampant victories against impossible odds and so a team of Sidereals must figure out how to bring down someone that makes First Age Solars look like pansies.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe the game is more focused on nation building and the consequences of hubris when wielding great power and one of the players wants to try applying Charms that don't do things in small ways to try to handle the subtle problems of ruling a nation. Maybe the idea of trying to keep their plans on track despite their super-player over-shooting the mark constantly sounds like an interesting problem to the other players. I've already heard of games where it was &quot;One Solar and four Dragon-Blooded&quot;, where the four Dragon-Blooded dealt with subtlety and the Solar player was employed as the trump card in their plans.<br /> <br /> The Exigence is a giant &quot;fill in the blank&quot; card in the setting. It can produce whatever odd situation you'd like to see happen. Want a nation whose military power comes from a cadre of vampire wolfmen? Need a reward great enough to entice a player into a deal with the a devil? Want a village guarded from outsiders by a lineage of blind swordsmen? If the toolbox of spirits, sorcery, demenses, and Wyld mutation can't get the job done, the Exigence probably can, especially with &quot;black market&quot; Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:06:01-08:00","id":1009955,"title":"","content":"Actually the Exigent book might be overkill for an Animal Avatar, make a non-QC version of an animal give it an essence pool that it can use to fuel it's own Magical Abilities that it learns like charms + port in some of the more basic effects like Ox Body etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe invert the Familiar Background to provide a human 'priest' who can understand you and relay your wishes to your allies if you want to seem a bit other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-29-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:37:23-08:00","id":1009972,"title":"","content":"I do think there's something interesting in the idea of an Animal Avatar as being a kind of legendary animal like Moby Dick or the special hunts in several Far Cry games, and using the existing rules for heir greatest and uncommon capabilities to cover that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T18:54:51-08:00","id":1010024,"title":"","content":"So, I fully approve of the idea of non-human exigents, at least in the case of things being run as NPCs. I'll likely veto ones trying to be run as PCs in things like the PbP I am running, if only for the reason of 'interacting with people', but in certain campaigns even they might be allowed, especially if it was set in somewhere like Halta, and the rest of the party was cool with it. But I actually had a villain who later turned ally be an animal Exigent.<br /> <br /> See, Loquesh, God of Sea Life, tired of his post in Heaven after the Usurpation, and gave up his titles in the celestial halls, to go and live with those who he had tended to and loved since the time of the Primordials. He made a home in the North-ish West, deep in the ocean, where he created a society of sea life both animal, beastmen [saving the children of Lunars who fell during the Usurpation was one of the reasons he left originally], and his own children, intelligent godblooded animals and humans alike. And then the Deathlords appeared, hundreds of years later. Loquesh was no god of Battle, but the Silver Prince ripped out of the underworld, and took over less than a day's swim away from where Loquesh's underwater society lay.<br /> <br /> And they were advancing, on dark boats with spirits of death upon them, unknowingly traveling over his head. Tainting his waters. And so Loquesh held a contest, to all creatures of his land, to find His Champion. A contest of skill, wit, strength, and general prowess, where the winner would receive his essence, contained within an Exigence, granted by his former friend, the Unconquered Sun, in this time of need.<br /> <br /> Against all odds, a normal, simple Dolphin, who understood the importance with no more intelligence than any of her kind... bested every opponent, Beastman, Godblooded, even great underwater predators. It proved cunning and capable, and was infused with the essence of Loquesh, becoming the Chosen of Sea Creatures. It was only after being bestowed the exigence that it gained human-like intelligence to begin with - though Loquesh could communicate with sea animal life much like Survival Solars could - but this consumed Loquesh. So Iiiiiqiiiii was created, and became leader of this underwater nation - where she began to defend her home against any entry from the Deathlord's, turning the zone into a veritable 'here thar be dragons' on Skullstone's maps. Out of the way enough to be deemed insignificant to fight, years of guerilla warfare lead to the Deathlord abandoning routes leading over her home.<br /> <br /> And left her with no idea what to do with herself. And so she became the leader, with no idea how to lead. The Loqueshans, previously saviors of drowning mortals became isolationist, sinking the ships of <i>anyone</i> daring to enter their domain, led by their great leader who possessed the might of every creature of the sea.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then the party, thrown off course after a battle they nearly died in, against the Silver Prince's fleet... wandered into Her territory.<br /> <br /> Long story short, after a few sessions, they all became friends and allies, and worked together to defeat Skull Stone completely. But before that, she nearly killed them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I probably broke setting 'rules' with making this story and character, but the key fact is that <i>I didn't care</i>. It made for a fun story that my players really enjoyed playing with, and they all really liked Iiiiqiiii [partly because of how I said their name, and voiced them in general.. It was very squeaky...] and I was glad I did it. And if the Exigent book, coming sometime after the next Epoch, tells me this is impossible, I'll still do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 11-29-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T22:36:16-08:00","id":1010065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009838#post1009838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your Storyteller thinks that such an Exigent serves his narrative needs or that giving such power to a player would create the kind of game he wants to run, then it is perfectly within the orbit of the Exigence to introduce such an Exalt to the game.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Celestial God of Victory burns herself out to empower a mortal general to triumph against all odds because she could not bear the thought of him dying defeated and that creates an Exalt with powers to literally say &quot;I win&quot; on nearly anything. Maybe this general is now threatening the design of fate because of his rampant victories against impossible odds and so a team of Sidereals must figure out how to bring down someone that makes First Age Solars look like pansies.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe the game is more focused on nation building and the consequences of hubris when wielding great power and one of the players wants to try applying Charms that don't do things in small ways to try to handle the subtle problems of ruling a nation. Maybe the idea of trying to keep their plans on track despite their super-player over-shooting the mark constantly sounds like an interesting problem to the other players. I've already heard of games where it was &quot;One Solar and four Dragon-Blooded&quot;, where the four Dragon-Blooded dealt with subtlety and the Solar player was employed as the trump card in their plans.<br /> <br /> The Exigence is a giant &quot;fill in the blank&quot; card in the setting. It can produce whatever odd situation you'd like to see happen. Want a nation whose military power comes from a cadre of vampire wolfmen? Need a reward great enough to entice a player into a deal with the a devil? Want a village guarded from outsiders by a lineage of blind swordsmen? If the toolbox of spirits, sorcery, demenses, and Wyld mutation can't get the job done, the Exigence probably can, especially with &quot;black market&quot; Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhile I will agree that the Exigents will fill whatever role one needs them to fill there will still be some obvious limitations on the power that can be given. There really is no way that the mechanics of the system will allow for a player to create an Exigent that can defeat any opponent with ease... because that would make the setting more or less pointless... as such a character could never loose... and having such a character as an antagonist means that no one that goes up against it could ever win... not the Solars... not even the Unconquered Sun (and I seriously doubt that the Unconquered Sun would ever allow any God to create an Exigent that could beat him... even if another Incarna were to sacrifice their existence to do so).<br /> <br /> \u200bExigents are not meant to be an &quot;I WIN!!!&quot; button for the game... but rather a means to allow Exalts that don't fit into the standard Solar, Lunar, Sidereal or Dragon-Blooded molds to exist. The requirements to create the Ultimate Exalt that can not be defeated by anyone or anything is likely so high that it may as well not be considered.<br /> <br /> \u200bAdditionally, we don't know what is needed to empower an Exigent. Yes, we are given an example of a God of the Harvest sacrificing its very existence to empower a single Exigent (who's power level we do not know), but we are also given examples of other Exigents... at least two of which likely didn't result in the spirit empowering them sacrificing their existence to do so (unless they've decided that Plentimon and Shalrina no longer exist... which there has been no mention of). The power levels of these Exigent examples have not been described in any significant way... within the setting or outside of it (actual mechanics). Even the one example provided in the Antagonists section suggests that this lone example is somewhere between Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal in power (going by the amount of Essence at her disposal), and her charms seem to reinforce this assessment.<br /> <br /> \u200bThus, saying that any level of power is possible without the information to back up such a claim is both foolish and very inaccurate. Yes, it might be possible once we are given the rules for creating Exigents... but until then we can't make that assumption. Just because something can be thought of, doesn't mean it will be possible to do. One of the few things that has been stated on the subject is that it may be possible to create an Exigent that is more powerful than a Solar, but in a very narrow field... which is true of most Exalts. Abyssals will be better at Necromancy than Solars ever will be... and their necrotic charms to drain essence from opponents and inflict penalties on them is also likely beyond what Solars can do. The same is true of Lunar Shapeshifting, Sidereal target number reduction or the Dragon-Blooded's connection to the base elements. In this manner, an Exigent could surpass a Solar in a very narrow field... such as Crafting... or Movement... or any single Ability or Attribute. This is because of the God's purview over such an area. To Create an Exigent so powerful that it could backhand both the Unconquered Sun and Malfeas at the same time with ease would require a God who's purview conceivably covers such an ability... a God theoretically more powerful that either the Unconquered Sun or Malfeas... of which there isn't (if there were, it would lead the Incarna and the Primordial War would likely have been won with ease). Even your Celestial God of Victory example would be limited... by what is considered a Victory... the Ultimate General may be victorious in any battle... but what of other areas that aren't related to war and fighting... such as winning the hearts of the people (social combat) or criminal endeavors (where stealth and underhandedness are more often the decider of victory than one's skill with a blade)? Not every General is a likeable person... nor skilled in atypical fighting. He might never be defeated in battle... but is only so when people fight him... go after any other target and<br /> <br /> \u200bExigents will be able to do many things that other Exalts may or may not be able to do... in ways that other Exalts usually can't... but what and how they do this is still a big unknown. Saying &quot;Yes&quot; to even the wildest and most game-breaking ideas with no knowledge of what will actually be possible is like giving someone a blank check to cash without knowing how much is in your account before hand... they may take only a little... or try to take more than you can actually cover.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo put it at its most basic... we really have no idea what the Exigents will be able to do... and how much it will cost the Gods that empower them. To say anything other that &quot;We don't know&quot; is just setting people up for huge disappointment if the power levels of Exigents turns out to be anything less than we imagine them to be (and going by your posts... you imagine them to be the most powerful Exalts ever... or at least have the potential to be, and won't be satisfied if they are anything less than that). I do hope that when we do get to the Exigents... you won't be disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:03:31-08:00","id":1010082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009972#post1009972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think there's something interesting in the idea of an Animal Avatar as being a kind of legendary animal like Moby Dick or the special hunts in several Far Cry games, and using the existing rules for heir greatest and uncommon capabilities to cover that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really depends on the animal in question. That works great with animals which have proven to be dangerous to humans when you can play up Jurassic Park levels of predatory intellect, but I don't really want the Killer Rabbit of Caerbannog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:41:30-08:00","id":1010138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1010082#post1010082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really depends on the animal in question. That works great with animals which have proven to be dangerous to humans when you can play up Jurassic Park levels of predatory intellect, but I don't really want the Killer Rabbit of Caerbannog.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn terms of interaction with humans rather than other rabbits and similarly sized animals, I would be inclined for a legendary rabbit to be less General Woundwort and more El-ahrairah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:10:21-08:00","id":1010245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1010065#post1010065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really is no way that the mechanics of the system will allow for a player to create an Exigent that can defeat any opponent with ease...</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be expecting hard rules about Exigents. The most that has been promised is a pile of guidelines about how to make new Charms without those Charms disrupting the game's balance assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bExigents are not meant to be an &quot;I WIN!!!&quot; button for the game... but rather a means to allow Exalts that don't fit into the standard Solar, Lunar, Sidereal or Dragon-Blooded molds to exist. The requirements to create the Ultimate Exalt that can not be defeated by anyone or anything is likely so high that it may as well not be considered. </div> </div> </div>You seem to be arguing against a position that I'm not taking. If you'd like to keep beating up your straw man, please continue, but no one is saying that Storytellers must allow Exigents that are more powerful than Solars to exist in their game. I only claim that this is a valid use case of Exigents for some tables.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThus, saying that any level of power is possible without the information to back up such a claim is both foolish and very inaccurate. </div> </div> </div>You haven't kept up with the developer statements on this, have you? All of the statements about the Exigence reinforce the idea that it is an explanation for whatever Exalt you want to come up with. They have stated that the power levels of Exigents can go from below that of Dragon-Blooded upward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saying &quot;Yes&quot; to even the wildest and most game-breaking ideas with no knowledge of what will actually be possible is like giving someone a blank check to cash without knowing how much is in your account before hand... they may take only a little... or try to take more than you can actually cover. </div> </div> </div>The Exigence is a creative blank check attached to a infinite bank account. It is a blank canvas upon which to draw up whatever idea takes your fancy and which will work in your game. Even &quot;game-breaking&quot; ideas are possible, because those &quot;game-breaking&quot; effects will be contained at your particular table and no one else has to deal with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To say anything other that &quot;We don't know&quot; is just setting people up for huge disappointment if the power levels of Exigents turns out to be anything less than we imagine them to be </div> </div> </div>But we do know. Exigents will range the full gamut of power ranges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (and going by your posts... you imagine them to be the most powerful Exalts ever... or at least have the potential to be, and won't be satisfied if they are anything less than that). </div> </div> </div>You really should make sure you aren't jousting at a straw man if you want to be taken seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do hope that when we do get to the Exigents... you won't be disappointed. </div> </div> </div>The only thing I could be disappointed by is the fluff and so far this edition has knocked the fluff out of the park on everything that isn't in the Charms chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:41:37-08:00","id":1010330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1009346-can-a-san-animal-become-an-exigents?p=1009359#post1009359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo\">Kyeudo</a>: </b>Not to be a dick but &quot;You can if you want to&quot; is kind of a useless answer in an RPG. Because anything can be if the GM wants it to. We have rules to provide a degree of mutual structure to guide what can be expected.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla\">webkilla</a>: That is totally epic.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}